{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-projective-line-object","@type":["folio-assistant-core:Definition","doco:Section"],"label":"def:projective-line-object","kind":"definition","title":"Projective line object","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-maximal-torus"],"examples":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/ex-projective-line-su2"],"tags":["projective-line"],"leanRef":"qou:QOU.ProjectiveLineObject","text":"projective-line-object.md","leanSource":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/projective-line-object.lean","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"def:projective-line-object\"></a><p>Let <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">(\\mathbf{C}, A, \\tau)</code> be a quantum observable universe. The <strong>projective line object</strong> is the quotient <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathbb{P}(V) = G / T</code>, realized in the category via its function algebra <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">A^{\\mathrm{co}T}</code>, the <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">T</code>-coinvariant subalgebra of <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">A</code>. Under the canonical fibre functor, it manifests as the scheme-theoretic projective line <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathbb{P}^1(R)</code>.</p>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/projective-line-object.md","leanStatus":"proved","heading":"Definition","number":"3.5.6"}
